1. Definitions
==============

"Software" means the Consent SDK source code, object code, associated
Documentation, bindings and any Modifications, in the form made available by
Licensor. A "Modification" is governed separately by this License and does not,
by itself, transfer ownership of Licensor's Intellectual Property.

"Documentation" means any technical specification, user manuals, or operational
guidelines Licensor provides describing the Software.

"You / Licensee" means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under
this License.

"Proof Object" means any cryptographically signed data object, token, or
payload generated by or derivedfrom the Software attesting to identity, legal
basis, consent, or authorization status.

"Affiliate" means, with respect to a party, any entity that directly or
indirectly controls, is controlled by, or is under common control with that
party, where "control" means ownership of more than 50% of the voting
securities or the power to direct management and policies, whether by contract
or otherwise.

"Production Deployment" means any use or installation of the Software (or any
Modification) that:

(a) Interacts with or provides services to any third party (including external
    end-users, clients, or microservices); or

(b) Generates, issues, validates, or consumes Proof Objects outside Licensee’s
    isolated, internal, non-production test environment.

"Commercial Purpose" means any use of the Software or any Modification other
than solely for non-production internal evaluation, research, development, and
non-commercial testing expressly permitted under Clause 2, including:

(a) any Production Deployment;

(b) any use of the Software or any Modification to generate, issue, validate,
    consume, or rely upon a Proof Object in a production or live environment,
    including any production key request or other non-sandbox execution;

(c) any provision of the Software, any Modification, or functionality
    materially derived from the Software to or for the benefit of any third
    party, whether a fee is charged or not; or

(d) any Competing Use.

For the avoidance of doubt, a use may constitute a Commercial Purpose
regardless of whether the Licensee or any third party receives monetary
consideration, and regardless of the Licensee's corporate structure, revenue,
employee count, or subjective intent. Use solely within an isolated,
non-production environment for internal evaluation, research, development, or
testing does not constitute a Commercial Purpose, provided that such use does
not constitute a Competing Use

"Competing Use" means using the Software, any Modification, or any Confidential
information derived from Licensee's access to the Software to build, offer,
license, or support a product, service, or component that (i) would, if made,
used, sold, offered for sale, or imported without a license, infringe any claim
of a Licensor Patent, or (ii) implements the specific consent-signal
architecture disclosed in the Software or Documentation (namely,
cryptographically-verifiable, third-party-issued proof objects mediating
personal-data-processing choices between a client system and a remote system).
Competing Use does not include developing products or services that fall
outside the scope of the Licensor Patents and do not implement the specific
architecture described above -even where such products address a similar
business problem or appear on Licensor's current or future public product
roadmap.

"Modification" means any revision, adaptation, translation, binding, or
derivative work of the Software prepared by or for Licensee.

"Licensor Patents" means (i) U.S. Patent No. 12,413,397 B2; (ii) European
Patent No. 4,100,905 B1 and any national patent rights deriving from that
European patent; and (iii) Chinese Patent Application No. CN115151937A and any
patent issuing therefrom; and (iv) any other patent application now or
hereafter owned or controlled by Licensor and covering the Software or its use,
together with any patent that issues, and any continuation, divisional,
reissue, continuation-in-part, reexamination, or foreign counterpart of any
patent or application identified in (i) through (iv), in each case to the
extent owned or controlled by Licensor and covering the Software or its use.
Licensee acknowledges that patent applications identified above are pending and
